{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Pending contract escalation — silt-resistant-gonolek (b0a8-5496-d178-40a9): raw package-free execution of private `_concurrency.py` regressed at d9e0f0e733 and now raises `ModuleNotFoundError`, but every supported production/library/subprocess route establishes `rebar_reconciler` package context before `applier._load_concurrency()` and succeeds; the caller census found no other route and canonical adapter identity is already singular. Exact decision: must every location-pinned/by-file-loaded reconciler module execute without package context, or only modules that explicitly declare and bootstrap a standalone contract? Recommendation: require context-free execution only for explicitly bootstrapped standalone modules. “Location-pinned” in ADR 0083 describes filesystem coupling, not a public entry-point promise; `_concurrency.py` is private, says it is inert on its own, and cannot be reached through applier without package context. Under this choice, classify silt-resistant-gonolek as `misunderstanding` / not-a-bug and close without code. If the operator instead wants universal context-free execution, approve that as a new package-wide contract and resume this ticket with the canonical dotted `lazy_load` repair plus an explicit contract test."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787051873443933001,"uuid":"b48e098a-e634-4759-9ac6-2174d904d92d"}